a tree with n nodes will have n-1 edges(connection btw 2 nodes).
graph is also a tree iff all the vertices are connected.
Degree-total no of children a node has is called its degree.
Degree of a tree is the highest value of the degree among all nodes 
Internal nodes-the node which has atleast 1 children is called internal node
Leaf node-the node which has no children is called leaf node.
Levels-In tree, each step from top to bottom is called level.
Height of a node-Longest path from that node to the leaf node (count no of edges)
Height of tree-Longest Path from root node to the last leaf node
Depth of a tree-It is reverse of Height 

Tpes of trees-
1.Regular tree
2.Binary tree
3.Binary Search tree

Binary tree-In binary tree each node must have atmost 2 children.
Binary Search tree- root > left node, root < right node
